        <section id="control-flow" >
          
            <h2>Control flow</h2>
              <p>Control flow is the order in which a computer executes statements in a script.</p>
<p>Code runs from the first line to the last unless the computer comes across structures like conditionals and loops which change the control flow.</p>
<p>For example say a script is used to validate user data for a webpage but if a field is left empty the script prompts them to fill it in.   The script uses a conditional structure so different code will be executed. Javascript amongst others includes many control structures including conditionals, loops and functions.</p>
<p>Control flow means that when a script is read, it must be read from start to finish, but also the program structure should be read so as to know how it affects the order of execution.</p>
<p>Control Flow is often represented in a control flow graph (CFG) during the execution of programs or applications.</p>
<p>Take a look at our <em>Javascript example</em> again and see if you can follow the control flow:</p>

              
              <div class="c-code"><pre class="language-js"><code class="language-js"><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment">// Declare some variables</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">var</span> variable_1 <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">25</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">var</span> variable_2 <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">28</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">var</span> list_1 <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token punctuation">[</span><span class="token number">5</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">2</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">6</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">3</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">7</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token number">2</span><span class="token punctuation">]</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment">// A conditional statement</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">if</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span>variable_1 <span class="token operator">===</span> variable_2<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">{</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">  console<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">log</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'the variables are equal.'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token punctuation">}</span> <span class="token keyword">else</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">  console<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">log</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'the variables are not equal.'</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token punctuation">}</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment">// A type of iteration (a loop)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">for</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token keyword">let</span> i <span class="token operator">=</span> <span class="token number">0</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span> i <span class="token operator">&lt;</span> list_1<span class="token punctuation">.</span>length<span class="token punctuation">;</span> i<span class="token operator">++</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">  console<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">log</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'List item '</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> i<span class="token punctuation">,</span> <span class="token string">' = '</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> list_1<span class="token punctuation">[</span>i<span class="token punctuation">]</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token punctuation">}</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment">// A function</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token keyword">function</span> <span class="token function">myFunction</span> <span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token parameter">input_1<span class="token punctuation">,</span> input_2</span><span class="token punctuation">)</span> <span class="token punctuation">{</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line">  sum_of_inputs <span class="token operator">=</span> input_1 <span class="token operator">+</span> input_2</span><br><span class="highlight-line">  console<span class="token punctuation">.</span><span class="token function">log</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span><span class="token string">'The sum of inputs = '</span><span class="token punctuation">,</span> sum_of_inputs<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token punctuation">}</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token comment">// A function call</span></span><br><span class="highlight-line"></span><br><span class="highlight-line"><span class="token function">myFunction</span><span class="token punctuation">(</span>variable_1<span class="token punctuation">,</span> variable_2<span class="token punctuation">)</span><span class="token punctuation">;</span></span></code></pre>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
        <section id="result" >
          
            <h2>Result</h2>
              
              <div class="c-code"><pre class="language-text"><code class="language-text"><span class="highlight-line">The variables are not equal</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List item 0 = 5</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List item 1 = 2</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List item 2 = 6</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List item 3 = 3</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List item 4 = 7</span><br><span class="highlight-line">List item 5 = 2</span><br><span class="highlight-line">The sum of inputs = 53</span><br><span class="highlight-line">[Finished in 192ms]</span></code></pre>
</div>

            
              <p>Note that in JavaScript coding language, the first index value starts at 0 not 1.</p>

          
